/home/axel/Archon-Horizon/docs/configuration/README.md-138-| `options.retry_base_seconds` | Base backoff delay in seconds for the retry above (default `8`; doubles each attempt). |
/home/axel/Archon-Horizon/docs/configuration/README.md:139:| `options.inbox_hooks` | Model-visible lifecycle checkpoints for Claude Code and Codex (default `true`). Horizon injects new messages after the next **mutating** tool boundary (not every Read/Grep), reminds sparingly while attention remains open, pauses a Bash commit for an unread direct conversation, and continues headless `Stop` once when conversations, uncommitted durable changes, or the final report still need attention. The second Stop always succeeds to prevent a loop. Hooks use a fast process entry (`agent-hook-fast`) so a no-op boundary stays cheap. Set `false` for an older or policy-locked engine. |
