r does. If you are staring at a naturality square you cannot close, check whether you built the map degreewise when a whiskered transformation was available.\" 2>&1 | tail -2; echo \"=== COMMIT ===\"; cd /home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon; \"$HORIZON_GIT\" read-tree HEAD >/dev/null 2>&1; \"$HORIZON_GIT\" commit --allow-empty -m \"THE COSIMPLICIAL NATURALITY OBLIGATION DOES NOT EXIST: whisker the mate, do not build degreewise\n\nCHECKPOINT of a verified probe result, before I rewire the file.\n\nr1 reported the two cosimplicial naturality squares as needing 'per-sigma projection lemmas\nnobody has built', because Pi.hom_ext cannot fire: the sigma-decomposition is buried mid-chain\nbehind pushforward/pullback applications. That diagnosis is correct ABOUT THE DEGREEWISE\nCONSTRUCTION -- and the degreewise construction is the mistake.\n\nWHAT I VERIFIED (LSP clean):\n\n (1) openImmersion_bareBC is MISNAMED. Its own docstring says it needs no open immersion and\n     no flatness -- it is the mate of the pullback-pseudofunctor 2-iso for any commuting\n     square. Instantiated at the OUTER square h : IsPullback g' f' f g it typechecks and gives\n        outerBC : pushforward f >> pullback g ==> pullback g' >> pushforward f'\n     a NATURAL TRANSFORMATION of functors X.Modules => S'.Modules.\n\n (2) The two sides of cech_pushforward_baseChange_natIso are DEFEQ (rfl, both directions\n     checked) to N >> (pushforward f >> pullback g) and N >> (pullback g' >> pushforward f')\n     for N = drop.obj (CechNerve U F). The nested CosimplicialObject.whiskering IS composition.\n\n (3) Therefore Functor.whiskerLeft N outerBC is a map between exactly those two cosimplicial\n     objects, and its naturality in the simplex index is outerBC's own naturality -- FREE, no\n     obligation. Promote with NatIso.isIso_of_isIso_app + asIso and the WHOLE residue becomes\n        forall n, IsIso (outerBC.app (N.obj n))\n     one IsIso per degree, no cosimplicial content whatsoever.\n\nSo 