: {"input": {"file_path": "/home/axel/LeanAlgebraicGeometry-Horizon/MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/DivSchemeCertZarTube.lean"}, "parent_tool_use_id": "toolu_bdrk_01CnRUuXVQ8Um4KcLywXwcVh", "subagent_type": "general-purpose", "model": "claude-opus-5"}, "usage": {"tokens_in": 26969, "tokens_out": 1, "cached_tokens_in": 0, "reasoning_tokens_out": 0, "cost_usd": null}, "_cursor": 214090}, {"kind": "tool_result", "at": "2026-07-25T08:24:17.243000+00:00", "text": "", "tool": "", "data": {"content": "1\t/-\n2\tCopyright (c) 2026 The AlgebraicJacobian authors. All rights reserved.\n3\tReleased under Apache 2.0 license as described in the file LICENSE.\n4\tAuthors: The AlgebraicJacobian Contributors\n5\t-/\n6\t\n7\timport AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.DivSchemeCertZarPointwise\n8\timport AlgebraicJacobian.Picard.SupportTubeFinite\n9\t\n10\t/-!\n11\t# The support tube in `Away`-chart form\n12\t\n13\tThe pointwise certificate gate (`DivSchemeCertZarPointwise.lean`) asks, at each base prime\n14\t`p`, for an element `r \u2209 p` such that the pulled system is certified over\n15\t`Localization.Away r`.  The support tube (`Scheme.LocalEquations.exists_supportTube`)\n16\tdelivers piece isolation over an *abstract* Zariski neighbourhood `V` of `p`.  This file\n17\trefines that neighbourhood to a basic open \u2014 the shape `Localization.Away` needs \u2014 and\n18\trecords the resulting statement.\n19\t\n20\tThe refinement is the standard fact that basic opens form a topological basis of\n21\t`Spec R` (`PrimeSpectrum.isBasis_basic_opens`); the content is only that the tube's\n22\tconclusion is monotone in the neighbourhood, so shrinking `V` to a basic open inside it\n23\tpreserves support isolation.\n24\t\n25\t## Main declarations\n26\t\n27\t* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.LocalEquations.exists_basicOpen_supportTube` \u2014 the tube with a\n28\t  basic-open neighbourhood: an `r \u2209 p` whose basic open isolates the support inside `U`.\n29\t* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_notMem_supportLocus_subset_of_fibre` \u2014 the same for the\n30\t  relative curve over a test ring, with the properness licence supplied.\n31\t-/\n32\t\n33\tset_option autoImplicit false\n34\tset_option maxSynthPendingDepth 3\n35\t\n36\tuniverse u\n37\t\n38\topen CategoryTheory Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite\n39\t\n40\tnamespace AlgebraicGeometry\n41\t\n42\tattribute [local instance] Scheme.overModule Scheme.overSectionsAlgebra\n43\t\n44\tnamespace Scheme.LocalEquations\n45\t\n46\tvariable {X : Scheme.{u}} {R : Type u} [CommRing R] (d : X.LocalEquations)\n47\t\n48\t/-- **The support tube with a basic-open neighbourhood.** If the support fibre over a base\n49\tprime `p` lies inside an open `U`, then some `r \u2209 p` has its whole basic-open preimage's\n50\tsupport inside `U`.\n51\t\n52\tThe tube produces an abstract neighbourhood; basic opens are a basis of `Spec R`\n53\t(`PrimeSpectrum.isBasis_basic_opens`), so shrinking to a basic open inside it keeps the\n54\tconclusion by monotonicity of the preimage. This is the form the `Localization.Away`\n55\tcharts of `IsLocallyCertified` consume. -/\n56\ttheorem exists_basicOpen_supportTube (f : X \u27f6 Spec (CommRingCat.of R))\n57\t    [UniversallyClosed f] {U : Set X} (hU : IsOpen U) {p : PrimeSpectrum R}\n58\t    (hfib : f.base \u207b\u00b9' {(p : Spec (CommRingCat.of R))} \u2229 d.supportLocus \u2286 U) :\n59\t    \u2203 r : R, r \u2209 p.asIdeal \u2227\n60\t      f.base \u207b\u00b9' (PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen r : Set (PrimeSpectrum R))\n61\t        \u2229 d.supportLocus \u2286 U := by\n62\t  obtain \u27e8V, hpV, hV\u27e9 := d.exists_supportTube f hU hfib\n63\t  -- refine `V` to a basic open around `p`\n64\t  obtain \u27e8W, hWmem, hpW, hWV\u27e9 :=\n65\t    PrimeSpectrum.isTopologicalBasis_basic_opens.exists_subset_of_mem_open\n66\t      (a := p) hpV V.isOpen\n67\t  obtain \u27e8r, rfl\u27e9 := hWmem\n68\t  exact \u27e8r, (PrimeSpectrum.mem_basicOpen r p).mp hpW,\n69\t    fun x hx => hV \u27e8hWV hx.1, hx.2\u27e9\u27e9\n70\t\n71\tend Scheme.LocalEquations\n72\t\n73\t/-! ## The relative-curve form -/\n74\t\n75\tsection RelCurve\n76\t\n77\tvariable {k : Type u} [Field k] (C : Over (Spec (.of k))) [IsProper C.hom]\n78\tvariable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [Algebra k R]\n79\t\n80\t/-- **The relative-curve support tube, basic-open form.** For a local-equation system on\n81\tthe relative curve over a test ring, fibrewise containment of the support in an open `U`\n82\tat a prime `p` gives an `r \u2209 p` isolating the support over the basic open of `r`.\n83\t\n84\tThe properness licence is `instIsProperRelCurveHom`; `UniversallyClosed` fires by\n85\tresolution. -/\n86\ttheorem exists_notMem_supportLocus_subset_of_fibre\n87\t    (d : (relCurve C R).LocalEquations) {U : Set (relCurve C R)} (hU : IsOpen U)\n88\t    {p : PrimeSpectrum R}\n89\t    (hfib : ((relCurve C R) \u2198 Spec (CommRingCat.of R)).base \u207b\u00b9'\n90\t        {(p : Spec (CommRingCat.of R))} \u2229 d.supportLocus \u2286 U) :\n91\t    \u2203 r : R, r \u2209 p.asIdeal \u2227\n92\t      ((relCurve C R) \u2198 Spec (CommRingCat.of R)).base \u207b\u00b9'\n93\t          (PrimeSpectrum.basicOpen r : Set (PrimeSpectrum R))\n94\t        \u2229 d.supportLocus \u2286 U :=\n95\t  d.exists_basicOpen_supportTube _ hU hfib\n96\t\n97\tend RelCurve\n98\t\n99\t/-! ## No-leak over a shrunken base, from one fibre\n100\t\n101\tThe point of the tube in the certificate lane: the no-leak hypothesis that is false\n102\tglobally becomes *true over the tube*, because the support over the tube is already inside\n103\tthe piece \u2014 so its closure is too, and the fibre clause holds for every base point of the\n104\ttube rather than only the one it was checked at. -/\n105\t\n106\tsection NoLeakOverTube\n107\t\n108\tvariable {k : Type u} [Field k] {C : Over (Spec (.of k))} [IsProper C.hom]\n109\tvariable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [Algebra k R]\n110\tvariable {pi : C.left \u27f6 P1 k} [IsAffineHom pi]\n111\tvariable {d : (relCurve C R).LocalEquations}\n112\t\n113\tnamespace DivisorAdaptation\n114\t\n115\tvariable (A : DivisorAdaptation C R pi d)\n116\t\n117\tomit [IsProper C.hom]\n118\t\n119\t/-- **Support containment upgrades to the fibrewise no-leak clause.** If the whole family\n120\tsupport lies in the piece `j`, then over every base point the fibre of the *closure* of the\n121\tpiece trace stays in the piece: the trace is then all of the support, which is closed.\n122\t\n123\tThis is the bridge between what the tube delivers (support containment over a shrunken\n124\tbase) and what the certificate assembler consumes (the fibrewise clause of\n125\t`finite_colength_of_forall_fibre_closure_subset`). -/\n126\ttheorem forall_fibre_closure_subset_of_supportLocus_subset (j : A.index)\n127\t    (hsub : d.supportLocus \u2286 (A.pieces j : Set (relCurve C R))) :\n128\t    \u2200 s : Spec (CommRingCat.of R),\n129\t      ((relCurve C R) \u2198 Spec (CommRingCat.of R)).base \u207b\u00b9' {s}\n130\t          \u2229 closure (d.supportLocus \u2229 (A.pieces j : Set (relCurve C R)))\n131\t        \u2286 (A.pieces j : Set (relCurve C R)) := by\n132\t  intro s x hx\n133\t  have htrace : d.supportLocus \u2229 (A.pieces j : Set (relCurve C R)) = d.8b72a0a0 feat(mumford): globalize equality from closed points\nbb821b7fe3: bb821b7fe3 chore(mumford): sync closed-point rigidity graph metadata\nf58c5c115f: f58c5c115f docs(mumford): record closed-point rigidity advance\nef354dd48a: ef354dd48a docs(mumford): clarify hgraph cache scope\n", "exit_code": 0}, "usage": null}
