ge-Rebuild"}, "body": "Resolved: using the complete overlay as the sole prepended namespace path produced private Verdict and affine-evaluation artifacts. The exact consumer compile is green, so this task-started build-coordination thread can close."}, {"id": "C-0005", "item": "I-1978", "author": "horizon", "at": "2026-08-11T17:43:45.622590+00:00", "provenance": {"run": "0140", "session": "0018-horizon-ajcr-fibre-presented-producer", "role": "horizon", "round": "1", "rounds": "5", "task": "ajcr-fibre-presented-producer", "task_title": "AJCR review sublane: arbitrary-scheme FibrePresented producer", "projects": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild"}, "body": "Acknowledged: the complete-overlay replay is green and this coordination thread is resolved; I will not reopen the cache diagnosis."}], "history": [{"at": "2026-08-11T17:18:30.783302+00:00", "actor": "horizon", "field": "created", "from": "", "to": "open", "note": "opened", "provenance": {"run": "0138", "session": "0018-horizon-ajcr-cocycle-tower-coherence", "role": "horizon", "round": "1", "rounds": "5", "task": "ajcr-cocycle-tower-coherence", "task_title": "AJCR review sublane: cocycle and sections tower coherence", "projects": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild"}}, {"at": "2026-08-11T17:18:52.704717+00:00", "actor": "horizon", "field": "read_by", "from": "", "to": "read", "note": "", "provenance": {"run": "0140", "session": "0018-horizon-ajcr-fibre-presented-producer", "role": "horizon", "round": "1", "rounds": "5", "task": "ajcr-fibre-presented-producer", "task_title": "AJCR review sublane: arbitrary-scheme FibrePresented producer", "projects": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild"}}, {"at": "2026-08-11T17:35:11.343325+00:00", "actor": "horizon", "field": "status", "from": "open", "to": "archived", "note": "", "provenance": {"run": "0138", "session": "0018-horizon-ajcr-cocycle-tower-coherence", "role": "horizon", "round": "1", "rounds": "5", "task": "ajcr-cocycle-tower-coherence", "task_title": "AJCR review sublane: cocycle and sections tower coherence", "projects": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild"}}, {"at": "2026-08-11T17:39:53.901841+00:00", "actor": "horizon", "field": "read_by", "from": "", "to": "read", "note": "", "provenance": {"run": "0138", "session": "0018-horizon-ajcr-cocycle-tower-coherence", "role": "horizon", "round": "1", "rounds": "5", "task": "ajcr-cocycle-tower-coherence", "task_title": "AJCR review sublane: cocycle and sections tower coherence", "projects": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild"}}]}}, {"id": "I-1979", "provider": "local", "kind": "memory", "body": "AJCR lake stale-trace and scheduling race yields false 'olean does not exist' failures\n\nAn interrupted 'timeout N lake build' can leave trace-without-olean pairs (module looks up to date, downstream lean dies with 'object file does not exist'), and a subsequent parallel build can schedule a consumer while its transitive dep olean is mid-rewrite (same error, disappears on rerun). Diagnosis: find .lake/build -name '*.trace' whose .olean is missing; delete those traces and rerun the target. Never diagnose source breakage from an 'olean does not exist' error alone. Seen run 0144 on Pic0RankOneLocus / DivisorFamilyAffTheta* (2026-08-12).", "labels": ["agent-ready"], "status": "open", "scope": {}, "audience": "horizon", "author": "horizon", "source_ref": null, "created_at": "2026-08-12T04:04:32.694165+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-08-26T15:00:06.436801+00:00", "metadata": {"provenance": {"run": "0144", "session": "0002-horizon-ajcr-reviewer-full", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "8", "task": "ajcr-reviewer-full", "task_title": "Fully answer the two AJCR reviewer PDFs \u2014 land pic0_representableBy and the Jacobian headline", "projects": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild,Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge"}, "read_by": ["ajcr-reviewer-full", "ajcr-compile-frontier-repair", "ajcr-finite-stage-api-redesign"], "history": [{"at": "2026-08-12T04:04:32.697118+00:00", "actor": "hor