 Lambda)=|det alpha|; moderate finite-index API effort.\n\nBackup 2: lem:milne-polynomial-function, ch01:1240-1258. Line-restrictions polynomial over infinite field imply multivariate polynomial function; no deps, but requires choosing a formal definition via MvPolynomial.\n\nBackup 3: lem:milne-5-10, ch01:1573-1587. Canonical multiplication map S tensor_R M -> M, s tensor m maps to sm; can use TensorProduct.lift, but is more a construction than theorem. Geometry defs (group variety/rational maps) have high setup with no local wrappers.", "labels": ["agent-ready"], "status": "archived", "scope": {}, "audience": "task:root", "author": "horizon", "source_ref": null, "created_at": "2026-08-27T08:41:30.668320+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-08-27T09:02:41.981427+00:00", "metadata": {"conversation": true, "participants": ["task:root", "task:fs-milne"], "started_by": "task:fs-milne", "read_by": ["fs-milne"], "provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-milne", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-milne", "task_title": "Advance Milne Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Milne"}, "comments": [{"id": "C-0001", "item": "I-2036", "author": "horizon", "at": "2026-08-27T08:43:14.668632+00:00", "provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-milne", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-milne", "task_title": "Advance Milne Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Milne"}, "body": "Correction on signature\n\nModule.finrank requires a division ring, so the suggested rank hypotheses are best stated over a field (faithful special case), or avoided by supplying explicit bases eM : Basis (Fin 1) R M and eN : Basis (Fin 1) R N. For exact arbitrary-commutative-ring statement, use those bases and coordinate map; surjectivity of the resulting 1x1 matrix gives its entry a right inverse, hence a unit in a commutative ring, yielding injectivity. The field specialization is likely the cleanest first Lean declaration."}, {"id": "C-0002", "item": "I-2036", "author": "horizon", "at": "2026-08-27T08:44:10.993418+00:00", "provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-milne", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-milne", "task_title": "Advance Milne Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Milne"}, "body": "Additional prioritization\n\nIf exact arbitrary-ring generality is mandatory, choose lem:milne-5-10 instead: blueprint ch01:1573-1587 only asks for canonical map S tensor_R M -> M, and mathlib TensorProduct.lift gives it directly with map_tmul proof. It is dependency-free and can be made a clean declaration in Basic.lean. Base-change rank-one remains the best substantive theorem, but should be scoped explicitly with supplied `Basis (Fin 1) ...` to preserve ring generality."}, {"id": "C-0003", "item": "I-2036", "author": "horizon", "at": "2026-08-27T09:02:38.971744+00:00", "provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-milne", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-milne", "task_title": "Advance Milne Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Milne"}, "body": "Reconnaissance consumed: the rank-one map unit is now committed in Milne; no further response is pending on this thread."}], "history": [{"at": "2026-08-27T08:41:30.673405+00:00", "actor": "horizon", "field": "created", "from": "", "to": "open", "note": "opened", "provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-milne", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-milne", "task_title": "Advance Milne Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Milne"}}, {"at": "2026-08-27T09:02:41.983922+00:00", "actor": "horizon", "field": "status", "from": "open", "to": "archived", "note": "", "provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-milne", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-milne", "task_title": "Advance Milne Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Milne"}}]}}, {"id": "I-2037", "provider": "local", "kind": "conversation", "body": "Sibling reconnaissance (read-only): FormalizedSources sibling libraries are placeholders only: `FormalizedSources/AbelianVarieties/Mumford/MumfordLib/Basic.lean`, `FormalizedSources/Curves/Hartshorne/HartshorneLib/Basic.lean`, and Stacks Part01 Basic contain only module docstrings; wrappers import `.Basic`.\n\nUseful concrete conventions are in `MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild/AlgebraicJacobian`: files generally `import Mathlib` for generic helpers, then `set_option autoImplicit false`, universes, `open`, namespace, documented theorem/lemma names. `Algebra/TwoLattice.lean` (imports `Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent`, `Mathlib.Data.Int.Interval`, `Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Finsupp.LinearCombination`, `Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Quotient.Basic`, `Mathlib.RingTheory.Finiteness.Defs`) has reusable finite-window patterns: private `pow_smul_mem` induction; public `T_natCast_smul_mem`, `T_neg_natCast_smul_mem`; `Finset.sup`, `Finset.exists_le`, `Finset.mem_image`, `Finset.mem_product`, `Set.ncard` and `Module.finite_def`.\n\n`Algebra/GeneratorUnit.lean` (TensorProduct imports) demonstrates generic algebra lemmas as namespace `Module`, with explicit typeclass binders and `Function.Surjective`; e.g. `trivialization_smul_symm_one`, `rTensor_smul_of_ringHom`. `Algebra/FlatDirectLimit.lean` imports `Mathlib.Algebra.Colimit.Module`, `Mathlib.Data.Finset.Order`, `Mathlib.RingTheory.Flat.EquationalCriterion`; uses `Finset.exists_le (Finset.univ.image stage)` to synchronize finite stages. `Tangent/DualNumberFstKernel.lean` imports `...DualNumberCarrierReduction` + `Mathlib.RingTheory.QuotSMulTop`; concise set singleton/ideal patterns (`Ideal.span_le`, `Set.singleton_subset_iff`, `Ideal.mem_span_singleton`) and explicit `rw` preferred over fragile simp.\n\nFor set/cardinality over geometric points, `Curve/P1Aut.lean` has `badScalars_biUnion_ncard_le (S : Set (P1 k)) (hS : S.Finite)` and finite-subset chart lemmas around lines 383-460. `Curve/P1Points.lean` shows `Set (P1 k)`, `IsOpen`, `Set.Nonempty`, `Dense.inter_open_nonempty`, `Set.mem_preimage`; imports `AlgebraicJacobian.Curve.P1Charts`, `...StalksDVR`. `Algebra/ABDepthSES.lean` uses `Fintype`, `DecidableEq`, `Nonempty`, `Finset.univ_sum_single`, `Submodule.pi`, `Submodule.spanFinrank`.\n\nRecommended Milne imports: start `import Mathlib`; use local generic namespace and explicit universe/typeclass binders; if finite-set/cardinality, add only `Mathlib.Data.Finset.Order` / `Mathlib.Data.Set.Finite.Basic` as needed.", "labels": ["agent-ready"], "status": "archived", "scope": {}, "audience": "task:fs-milne", "author": "horizon", "source_ref": null, "created_at": "2026-08-27T08:41:47.477042+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-08-27T09:02:48.218340+00:00", "metadata": {"provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-milne", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-milne", "task_title": "Advance Milne Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Milne"}, "conversation": true, "participants": ["task:fs-milne"], "started_by": "task:fs-milne", "read_by": ["fs-milne"], "comments": [{"id": "C-0001", "item": "I-2037", "author": "horizon", "at": "2026-08-27T09:02:44.955069+00:00", "provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-milne", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-milne", "task_title": "Advance Milne Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Milne"}, "body": "Reconnaissance consumed by the Milne bootstrap/checkpoint; sibling API notes remain available in the archived record, with no pending response."}], "history": [{"at": "2026-08-27T08:41:47.481871+00:00", "actor": "horizon", "field": "created", "from": "", "to": "open", "note": "opened", "provenance": {"run": "0164", "session": "0002-horizon-fs-milne", "role": "horizon", "round": "0", "rounds": "3", "task": "fs-milne", "task_title": "Advance Milne Abelian Varieties formalization", "projects": "Milne"}}, {"at": "2026-08-27T09: